1
00:05:21,176 --> 00:05:27,176
A hometown hero battles a giant corporation to save his city.

2
00:10:42,352 --> 00:10:48,352
Roger & Me is a documentary, history, comedy film directed by Michael Moore.

3
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:09,529
A documentary about the closure of General Motors' plant at Flint,
Michigan, which resulted in the loss of 30,000 jobs.

4
00:21:24,705 --> 00:21:30,705
Details the attempts of filmmaker Michael Moore to get
an interview with GM CEO Roger Smith.

5
00:26:45,882 --> 00:26:51,882
Self, played by Michael Moore.

6
00:32:07,058 --> 00:32:13,058
Self, played by Rhonda Britton.

7
00:37:28,235 --> 00:37:34,235
Self, played by Fred Ross.

8
00:42:49,411 --> 00:42:55,411
Self, played by Roger B. Smith.

9
00:48:10,588 --> 00:48:16,588
Self, played by Bob Eubanks.

10
00:53:31,764 --> 00:53:37,764
Self, played by James Blanchard.

11
00:58:52,941 --> 00:58:58,941
Roger & Me is a 1989 American documentary film written, produced, directed
by, and starring Michael Moore, in his directorial debut.

12
01:04:14,117 --> 01:04:20,117
Moore portrays the regional economic impact of General Motors CEO Roger Smith's action of closing several auto plants in his
hometown of Flint, Michigan, reducing GM's employees in that area from 80,000 in 1978 to about 50,000 in 1992.

13
01:09:35,294 --> 01:09:41,294
The film won the People's Choice Award at the 14th
Toronto International Film Festival.

14
01:14:56,470 --> 01:15:02,470
In 2013, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically or aesthetically significant".

15
01:20:17,647 --> 01:20:23,647
The film explores themes of capitalism,
economics, unemployment, corporate greed.

16
01:25:38,823 --> 01:25:44,823
The tone is lighthearted.
